Finding: {"title":"syncPaymentToQuickBooks discards existing invoiceUrl, destroying prior data on every payment sync","severity":"HIGH","area":"business-rules / data-integrity","files":["src/lib/quickbooks-sync.ts"],"detail":"In `syncPaymentToQuickBooks` (src/lib/quickbooks-sync.ts:409-413), after building `updatedMeta` from the existing parsed metadata, the code calls `buildQBUrl(null, updatedMeta)` instead of `buildQBUrl(invoice.invoiceUrl, updatedMeta)`. `buildQBUrl` (lines 77-83) preserves any pre-existing non-QB URL (e.g. a Stripe hosted invoice link) by prefixing it before the `qb:` metadata suffix, but only when the caller passes the existing URL. Passing `null` always collapses `invoiceUrl` down to just the bare `qb:{...}` JSON blob, silently wiping out whatever was stored before every time a payment is synced.","impact":"Any Stripe-hosted-invoice link or other data previously appended to `invoiceUrl` is permanently lost the first time a payment syncs to QuickBooks for that invoice. Downstream UI/consumers reading `invoiceUrl` for a Stripe link will silently break after payment sync.","recommendation":"Change line 412 to `buildQBUrl(invoice.invoiceUrl, updatedMeta)` so the existing URL prefix is preserved. Add a unit test that seeds `invoice.invoiceUrl` with both a plain URL and prior `qb:` metadata, syncs a payment, and asserts the original prefix survives.","confidence":"HIGH"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

